# DELIBERATELY OVER THE LIMIT. cbc must REFUSE this file.
#
# Generated fixture, kept because mutation testing proved the limit was untested: raising the vote expansion cap from 64 to 640
# in lower.cpp left all 42 tests passing. The guard could have been loosened or deleted and nothing would have
# noticed, which matters because past 31 observations the failure is SILENT -- binding's bit() returns 0 for any
# observation index >= 32, so those observations would never assert and the device would answer confidently with
# an incomplete picture of the world.
casebook vote_too_wide v1
source "generated fixture for the vote expansion cap" dated 2026-09-25 by "quorum"
observe lt0 "transmitter 0 reads high"
observe lt1 "transmitter 1 reads high"
observe lt2 "transmitter 2 reads high"
observe lt3 "transmitter 3 reads high"
observe lt4 "transmitter 4 reads high"
observe lt5 "transmitter 5 reads high"
observe lt6 "transmitter 6 reads high"
observe lt7 "transmitter 7 reads high"
observe lt8 "transmitter 8 reads high"
